      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Island instead of Steam Vents on turn 1 is slightly suboptimal. With Sleight of Hand in hand (a U sorcery to cast turn 1), the player wants to cast it this turn. Both Island and Steam Vents can produce U, but playing Steam Vents turn 1 (paying 2 life to have it enter untapped) is better because it preserves flexibility for future turns. The hand has no red cards currently, but Steam Vents entering tapped later could be costly when the player needs to hold up Spider-Sense or cast Winternight Stories on curve. Playing the shockland early when life is at 20 and the tempo cost is lowest is generally correct sequencing - you want to take shock damage early when it matters least, and save basic lands for later turns when entering tapped would be more punishing.",
