      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Island instead of Steam Vents is suboptimal. With Steam Vents, the player could pay 2 life to have it enter untapped, giving access to both blue and red mana. Playing a basic Island means one of the two Steam Vents will need to be played later, potentially when entering tapped would be more costly. More importantly, playing Steam Vents untapped now would give 2 blue sources to cast Opt or Sleight of Hand this turn while keeping Spider-Sense mana up. Playing Island achieves the same immediate mana but wastes a chance to diversify mana colors for future turns (Winternight Stories needs blue, but future red cards could matter). However, the more pressing issue is that playing a basic Island over Steam Vents means the player has slightly less flexible mana going forward - though the difference is small since they have two Steam Vents remaining.",
