      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 57,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Meticulous Archive (enters tapped) instead of Sunbillow Verge as the land drop. With 4 lands already on board (Hallowed Fountain, Plains, Floodfarm Verge, Sunbillow Verge), Sunbillow Verge would enter and can tap for W (since Plains is controlled) or R. Playing Sunbillow Verge untapped would leave 5 mana available, enough to cast Day of Judgment (2WW) with mana open. Playing Meticulous Archive tapped means only 4 mana available. While the surveil 1 from Archive has some value, the tempo loss of an enters-tapped land is notable. Additionally, the player could have played Sunbillow Verge and then cast Consult the Star Charts or held up No More Lies with 5 lands untapped. The surveil 1 is a minor upside but the tempo difference matters, especially when holding Day of Judgment and counter magic.",
      "action_taken": "Played Meticulous Archive (enters tapped) as land drop for turn 5.",
      "better_line": "Play Sunbillow Verge untapped instead, keeping 5 mana available to hold up Day of Judgment or No More Lies + other interaction. The surveil 1 is minor compared to having full mana available.",
