    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Rest in Peace could have been cast here to proactively exile graveyards and prevent future graveyard synergies. The opponent has Into the Flood Maw in their graveyard, and importantly, the opponent appears to be playing a blue deck that likely runs Eddymurk Crab (which costs less for each instant/sorcery in graveyard). Casting Rest in Peace now would be a proactive enchantment that provides ongoing value by exiling all future cards that would go to graveyards, making Eddymurk Crab much more expensive. Additionally, the opponent has 5 mana open including only blue sources, so countermagic is a concern - but passing with no development at all is also questionable when there's a proactive enchantment available.",
