    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Used the more flexible counterspell (Spider-Sense) when the narrow one (Spell Snare) would have worked perfectly. Spell Snare costs only {U} vs Spider-Sense's {1}{U}, saving 1 mana this turn. More importantly, Spider-Sense is a broader answer that hits any instant, sorcery, or triggered ability, while Spell Snare only hits MV 2 spells. Using the narrow answer when applicable preserves the flexible one for future threats. The player's reasoning was also incorrect - they claimed Spider-Sense draws a card, which it does not.",
