      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Consult the Star Charts during main phase when the opponent is tapped out wastes the opportunity to hold up countermagic (No More Lies) or removal (Get Lost) during the opponent's turn. With all of the opponent's lands tapped, this was a safe window, but Consult the Star Charts is an instant and could be cast at end of opponent's turn instead, preserving flexibility. More importantly, playing Hallowed Fountain first (from hand) before casting Consult would give 8 lands instead of 7, letting them look at one additional card. Additionally, Rest in Peace could be a strong proactive play here since the opponent has Spider-Sense, Glacial Dragonhunt, and Into the Flood Maw in their graveyard - Glacial Dragonhunt has Harmonize (castable from graveyard) and denying graveyard resources while the opponent is tapped out is valuable.",
