    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Eddymurk Crab is a 5/5 that costs {5}{U}{U} but gets {1} cheaper for each instant/sorcery in the graveyard. Sonnet Vorthos has 3 instants/sorceries in graveyard (Into the Flood Maw, Glacial Dragonhunt, Spider-Sense), so it costs {2}{U}{U} - very efficiently costed for a 5/5 that also taps up to two creatures on entry. This is a major threat that Kimi25 had multiple answers for. No More Lies would counter it unless opponent pays {3} (they have 5 lands but may not have 3 extra mana after casting the Crab for 4 mana - they'd have exactly 1 mana left, so they cannot pay {3}). Tishana's Tidebinder could counter the ETB trigger but still leaves a 5/5 on board. Get Lost could destroy it but gives two Map tokens. No More Lies was clearly the best option here - it would cleanly counter the Crab since the opponent tapped 4 of their 5 lands to cast it and cannot pay {3}. Instead, Kimi25 let a 5/5 resolve that will also tap two of their permanents.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority and let Eddymurk Crab resolve without using any of the three available answers.",
