      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 110,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Kimi25 has a 5/5 Eddymurk Crab on the opponent's board and 4 untapped lands. Get Lost costs {1}{W} and would destroy the Crab immediately. Instead, they passed without acting. While holding Tishana's Tidebinder for flash is reasonable in some contexts, the Crab is already on the battlefield - Tidebinder only counters activated/triggered abilities, not creatures already in play. The Crab's ETB trigger (tap up to two creatures) has presumably already resolved. Passing here means the Crab will be able to attack for 5 next turn. Get Lost at sorcery speed (main phase) cleanly removes it now, and the Map tokens given to the opponent are minor downside. They could cast Get Lost now and still have mana for Tidebinder or No More Lies on the opponent's turn.",
