      "description": "Kimi25 has a 5/5 Eddymurk Crab threatening them on the opponent's board. Get Lost cleanly destroys it for 2 mana, while Tishana's Tidebinder is a 3/2 flash creature that doesn't address the Crab at all (its ETB counters activated/triggered abilities, not creatures). The opponent has 4 tapped lands and only Riverpyre Verge untapped, so they likely can't protect the Crab. Deploying Tidebinder leaves the 5/5 Crab on board to attack next turn for a quarter of Kimi25's life total, while Get Lost would remove it immediately. The Map tokens given to the opponent are a minor downside compared to taking repeated 5/5 hits.",
