      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Kimi25 chose to cast Tishana's Tidebinder over Get Lost to deal with the opponent's Eddymurk Crab. Tidebinder is a 3/2 that counters activated/triggered abilities, but the Crab's ETB has already resolved. Tidebinder doesn't remove the 5/5 Crab - it just puts a 3/2 body on board that can't profitably block it. Get Lost would actually destroy the Crab, which is the main threat. However, Tidebinder does add a body to the board and preserves Get Lost for later, and Kimi25 also has Day of Judgment as a backup plan. The Crab represents a significant clock (5 damage per turn), so removing it now with Get Lost might be more urgent. That said, playing Tidebinder develops the board and keeps removal options open, so this is debatable.",
