    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Attacking with Tishana's Tidebinder (3/2) into an untapped Eddymurk Crab (5/5) is risky. The Crab can block and kill the Tidebinder without dying. Tishana's Tidebinder is a valuable creature that may be countering an ability, and trading it for nothing seems poor. However, the opponent has all lands tapped, so there are no combat tricks available. If the opponent blocks with Crab, Kimi loses the Tidebinder for no damage. If they don't block, 4 damage is significant. The opponent almost certainly blocks the Tidebinder with the Crab since taking 4 is painful at 14 life. Losing the Tidebinder means losing whatever ability it was suppressing. That said, the Fish token alone would deal 1 unblocked damage, and the Tidebinder could be held back. With Day of Judgment in hand, Kimi could just wrath next turn instead of trading the Tidebinder in combat.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with both Fish Token and Tishana's Tidebinder into an untapped 5/5 Eddymurk Crab",
      "better_line": "Attack with only the Fish Token (likely getting 1 damage through), keep Tidebinder back as a blocker or to maintain its ability-suppression effect, and plan to cast Day of Judgment next turn to cleanly answer the Eddymurk Crab",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 88,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 135,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
