    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Sunderflock before Opt is slightly suboptimal sequencing. Casting Opt first (and potentially finding something better or more information) before committing to Sunderflock would be better, especially since there's plenty of mana for both plus holding up Spell Snare. Additionally, deploying both major threats simultaneously exposes them to a single Day of Judgment, though Spell Snare can't counter it anyway (MV 4).",
      "action_taken": "Cast Sunderflock immediately as the first spell of the turn",
