      "decision_index": 147,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Kimi25 allowed Sunderflock (a 5/5 flyer that bounces all non-Elemental creatures) to resolve when they had No More Lies available with the mana to cast it. Sunderflock's ETB trigger will return the Fish token to hand (though that's minor). More critically, a 5/5 flyer is an enormous threat that will close the game quickly. Kimi25 has Day of Judgment in hand which could answer it, but spending a board wipe on a single creature is very inefficient, and the opponent likely has countermagic (they play blue). No More Lies would have countered Sunderflock unless the opponent paid 3 additional mana. Looking at the board, the opponent cast Sunderflock with Eddymurk Crab already on board (reducing its cost), and likely tapped most/all their lands, making it very difficult to pay the additional 3. This was a must-counter threat - a 5/5 flyer that also bounces non-Elementals.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Sunderflock with No More Lies, allowing a 5/5 flyer to resolve and bounce their Fish token.",
      "better_line": "Cast No More Lies targeting Sunderflock. The opponent likely couldn't pay the additional 3 mana, and even if they could, that would be a significant tempo loss. A 5/5 flyer is a game-ending threat that demands an answer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 94,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 150,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Kimi25 declined to cast Get Lost on either Eddymurk Crab (5/5) or Sunderflock (5/5 flyer) while having the mana to do so. The opponent has 10 power on board including a 5/5 flyer, representing a fast clock. While Kimi25 has Day of Judgment in hand, they only have 4 untapped lands (Plains, Sunbillow Verge, Meticulous Archive, Hallowed Fountain) and Day of Judgment costs 2WW - they can cast it next turn. However, Get Lost at instant speed could remove Sunderflock (the flying threat that's harder to block) right now, and Day of Judgment could clean up next turn if needed. The reasoning about 'not revealing their hand' makes no sense when facing 10 power of threats. More critically, Sunderflock's ETB trigger is about to bounce the Fish token (a minor loss), but the real issue is leaving two massive threats on board when you could efficiently answer one now. Not using Get Lost on the Sunderflock (which flies over blockers and is the more dangerous threat) is a meaningful missed opportunity.",
