    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 8 lands on the battlefield and no creatures from either player on board, the Villain declined to activate Cori Mountain Monastery's ability ({3}{R}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card). This is a pure card advantage ability that could be activated at the end of the opponent's turn, but since this is postcombat main phase with mana available and nothing else productive to do, activating it now is reasonable too. The opponent has no board presence, so there's no immediate need to hold up mana for removal spells. While the hand is already strong, declining a free card advantage activation when you have spare mana is leaving value on the table. The Villain could activate the Monastery and still hold up mana for No More Lies (WU) with the remaining untapped lands.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Cori Mountain Monastery or casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Activate Cori Mountain Monastery to exile the top card for future use, spending 4 mana (3R) while still keeping some lands untapped for countermagic like No More Lies or Spell Pierce on the opponent's turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 179,
