      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Burst Lightning during combat on an empty board with no attackers seems premature. The opponent is at 13 life, so two Burst Lightnings only deal 4 damage total (non-kicked). There's no reason to fire off burn spells now rather than holding them. Burst Lightning could be cast at end of opponent's turn to preserve the option of using mana for counterspells (Spell Snare, Spell Pierce) during the opponent's turn. Casting it during your own combat phase when you have no creatures attacking means you're tapping mana that could be held up for interaction on the opponent's turn.",
