    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos declined to counter either of two spells on the stack while having Spell Snare (which perfectly counters Consult the Star Charts, MV 2) and Spell Pierce available with untapped mana. At 9 life, letting Burst Lightning resolve for 2-4 damage while also letting the opponent draw cards from Consult the Star Charts is a significant value loss. At minimum, Spell Snare on Consult the Star Charts is a guaranteed counter that denies card advantage.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without countering either spell, letting both Burst Lightning and Consult the Star Charts resolve.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Consult the Star Charts to deny card advantage with a guaranteed counter, or attempt Spell Pierce on Burst Lightning to potentially prevent damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 213,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 318,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Consult the Star Charts (MV 2) is on the stack, and Kimi25 has Spell Snare which perfectly counters MV 2 spells for just {U}. Letting the opponent's card selection/advantage spell resolve for free when holding the ideal counter is a significant missed opportunity. Kimi25 has untapped Hallowed Fountain and Island to cast it.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, allowing both Burst Lightning and Consult the Star Charts to resolve without interaction.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Consult the Star Charts to counter the opponent's card advantage spell. The Burst Lightning for 2 damage is acceptable at 13 life, but giving the opponent free card selection is not.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 213,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 317,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Consult the Star Charts is a card advantage spell that will let the opponent dig through their library to find threats or answers. With 3 copies of No More Lies in hand and the mana to cast one (Hallowed Fountain and Island are untapped, providing W and U), Kimi25 should counter this spell. Letting the opponent draw cards when you have three counterspells in hand and the mana available is a significant missed opportunity, especially when the opponent is at 9 life and you need to prevent them from finding more threats while you have Day of Judgment as a safety valve.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Consult the Star Charts, passing priority.",
      "better_line": "Cast No More Lies targeting Consult the Star Charts. The opponent would need to pay 3 additional mana, and since most of their lands are tapped, they likely cannot pay, so the spell gets exiled. This denies card advantage and maintains your counter-heavy hand for future threats.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 214,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 320,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to counter Consult the Star Charts (MV 2) with Spell Snare when holding 3 copies. Letting the opponent look at top 8 cards and select the best one provides significant card advantage/selection. With 3 Spell Snares in hand, using one here is very reasonable since there's redundancy for future MV 2 threats.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Consult the Star Charts, letting opponent dig through top 8 cards for the best option.",
      "better_line": "Cast Spell Snare targeting Consult the Star Charts to deny the opponent significant card selection, still retaining 2 more Spell Snares for future MV 2 spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 214,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 318,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "In a control mirror at 11 vs 9 life with no win conditions in hand or on board, Kimi25 passed on Restless Anchorage - a creature-land that serves as a win condition while also being a free land drop. Their hand is already overloaded with 7 reactive cards (counters, removal, board wipe). Taking Stock Up to draw more reactive cards instead of the only available win condition is a significant strategic error.",
      "action_taken": "Selected Stock Up and Three Steps Ahead from Consult the Star Charts",
      "better_line": "Should have taken Restless Anchorage (win condition / free land drop) plus Three Steps Ahead. The deck desperately needs a way to actually win the game, not more card draw into more reactive spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 214,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 320,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed the main phase without casting Stock Up while opponent was completely tapped out. With 3 untapped lands (exactly enough for Stock Up's {2}{U} cost) and the opponent having zero mana available, this was a risk-free window to cast a sorcery. While Kimi25 already has 9 cards in hand (above hand size), the card selection from Stock Up (look at 5, keep 2) would help find win conditions they clearly need, since they appear to have no creatures on board. The reasoning about 'attacking' seems confused since Aang's Iceberg is an enchantment, not a creature.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the precombat main phase without casting any spells, seemingly to move to combat despite having no creatures to attack with.",
      "better_line": "Cast Stock Up with the 3 available mana while opponent is tapped out, getting valuable card selection to find threats, then discard excess cards at end of turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 215,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 321,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Sacrificed Aang's Iceberg for scry 2, which returns whatever permanent it was exiling back to the opponent's battlefield, AND taps out all remaining mana so no countermagic (No More Lies x3, Spell Snare) can be held up. The opponent is at 5 life - maintaining control with countermagic is critical. Scry 2 is marginal when the hand already has 7 cards of interaction.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Aang's Iceberg waterbend to sacrifice it for scry 2, tapping out remaining 3 mana",
      "better_line": "Pass without activating, keeping 3 mana up to hold No More Lies as countermagic during the opponent's turn. The Iceberg continues exiling a threat while counter protection is maintained.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 220,
      "player": "Kimi25 Villain",
      "decision_index": 326,
    }
  ],
